description:
**Overview**

**Building Code Compliance \& BIM/CAD Advisor – AI Innovation Project**  
**Contract / Part\-time / Advisory** 

**Location:** Greater Toronto Area / Ontario preferred; remote possible within Canada

Lextar AI Legal Solutions Inc. is an Ontario\-based AI company developing human\-supervised AI workflows for document\-heavy and rule\-heavy professional work.

We are exploring a Government of Canada innovation opportunity involving AI\-assisted compliance review for building permit applications. The project would involve applying AI to review building permit materials, 2D drawings, PDF/CAD drawings, and potentially BIM/IFC models against Canadian building\-code and permit\-review requirements.

Lextar AI can provide the AI workflow, rule\-mapping, explainable review, human\-in\-the\-loop process, and auditability design. We are seeking a construction\-code / building\-permit / BIM\-CAD domain expert to help us evaluate the opportunity, shape the proposal, and potentially participate in a prototype or funded project.

**Ideal background**

We are interested in candidates with experience in two or more of the following areas:

* National Building Code of Canada, Ontario Building Code, or other Canadian provincial building codes;
* building permit applications and municipal permit review;
* preparation or review of permit drawing sets;
* Part 3 and/or Part 9 building\-code compliance;
* occupancy classification, egress, fire separation, accessibility, spatial separation, or related code issues;
* AutoCAD, Revit, BIM, IFC, or digital construction workflows;
* building\-code compliance checklists, code matrices, plans review comments, or municipal deficiency comments;
* experience as an architect, P.Eng., architectural technologist, BCIN designer, building\-code consultant, BIM/Revit specialist, former plans examiner, or municipal building official.

**Possible responsibilities**

The selected candidate may help with:

* identifying building\-code compliance requirements suitable for AI\-assisted review;
* explaining how permit drawings are reviewed in practice;
* helping convert selected code requirements into structured rules, checklists, or test cases;
* reviewing sample drawing/BIM workflows;
* validating whether AI\-generated compliance findings are correct, incomplete, uncertain, or require human review;
* advising on practical permit\-review workflows used by municipalities or design professionals;
* supporting a government innovation proposal and, if successful, participating in a prototype or pilot.

**What we are looking for**

We are looking for someone who can bridge the gap between building\-code practice and AI\-assisted compliance review. You do not need to be an AI engineer. The key requirement is practical knowledge of construction\-code compliance, permit drawings, and how building officials or design professionals identify compliance issues.

**Engagement structure**

This role may begin as a short\-term consulting or advisory engagement. Depending on candidate fit, project status, funding, and mutual interest, it may develop into a longer\-term contract, full\-time role, subcontractor relationship, or strategic partnership.

Compensation and engagement structure will be discussed with shortlisted candidates based on experience, availability, and project scope.

**To apply**

Please send your resume or a short background summary, and briefly answer:

* Which Canadian building codes or permit\-review workflows are you most familiar with?
* Have you prepared or reviewed building permit drawings?
* Do you have experience with AutoCAD, Revit, BIM, or IFC?
* Have you worked with municipal plans review, code compliance comments, or permit deficiencies?
* Are you interested in a consulting role, full\-time role, partnership, or flexible arrangement?

Pay: $60\.00\-$80\.00 per hour

Benefits:

* Dental care
* Flexible schedule

Work Location: Hybrid remote in Toronto, ON (York District)

**Job Title: Machine Learning Engineer** 




**Location: Toronto, ON\- Hybrid** 




**Employment Type: Contract** 










 At Smart IT Frame, we connect top talent with leading organizations across the USA. With over a decade of staffing excellence, we specialize in IT, healthcare, and professional roles, empowering both clients and candidates to grow together.










**Responsibilities:** 




 • Experience building modular and robust software systems in Python or similar language;




 • Knowledge of professional software engineering best practices for the full software development life cycle, including testing methods, coding standards, code reviews and source control management;




 • Experience working across the entire ML\\GenAI research and product lifecycle from prototyping to production is a plus;




 • Experience building microservices, data pipelines and using relational and non\-relational databases is a plus;




 • Experience with Front\-end development and best practices is a plus;




 • Experience with DevOps engineering (CI/CD pipelines, observability, containers etc) is a plus.

At eBay, we're more than a global ecommerce leader — we’re changing the way the world shops and sells. Our platform empowers millions of buyers and sellers in more than 190 markets around the world. We’re committed to pushing boundaries and leaving our mark as we reinvent the future of ecommerce for enthusiasts.




 Our customers are our compass, authenticity thrives, bold ideas are welcome, and everyone can bring their unique selves to work — every day. We're in this together, sustaining the future of our customers, our company, and our planet.




 Join a team of passionate thinkers, innovators, and dreamers — and help us connect people and build communities to create economic opportunity for all.




**About The Team And The Role**
 The Search Query Science team at eBay is a key driver of the company's search revenue and is growing rapidly. We're building a world\-class team that values bold, innovative thinking and rewards impact. Our work focuses on solving core e\-commerce search challenges—like query rewriting, annotation, classification, and recovery—using cutting\-edge ML algorithms that interpret large\-scale user behavior. With a fun, collaborative environment, we're now looking for stellar applied researchers to develop advanced query understanding products. If you're excited by large\-scale query processing—intent detection, entity resolution, categorization, expansion and filter recommendation—join us and help redefine query understanding at eBay.




**What You Will Accomplish**
* Tackle advanced AI challenges in Query Science and NLP at eBay.
* Collaborate with researchers and engineers on cutting\-edge technologies.
* Contribute to solving complex problems that impact eBay's platform.
* Help shape the technical vision for query understanding.
* Apply software engineering best practices to improve development experience.
* Build offline data pipelines for ML model training and validation.
* Design and deploy web services for serving real\-time inference algorithms.


**What You Will Bring**
* A PhD in Machine Learning/AI or related fields, or at least two years of industry experience the field;
* Proven track record of applied research in AI/ML;
* Knowledge of Machine Learning and Statistics fundamentals: classification, regression, and clustering, dimensionality reduction and feature selection, convex/non\-convex optimization, ranking and recommendation, hypothesis sing;
* Strong education in computer science (data structures and algorithms, computational complexity analysis) and proficiency with one or more programming language (Python, Java, C/C\+\+, bash and other scripting languages);
* Experience or interest in working with all kinds of Artificial Neural Networks and Large Language Models;
* Experience or interest in working with service\-oriented architectures and frameworks (e.g. SpringBoot);
* Experience or interest in working with cloud computing solutions (Docker, Kubernetes, etc.);
* Proven ability to work independently and make good decisions with minimal direction;
* Strong communication skills (fluent English, both verbal and written)


**Additional Details**
 eBay is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, and disability, or other legally protected status. If you have a need that requires accommodation, please contact us at talent@ebay.com. We will make every effort to respond to your request for accommodation as soon as possible. View our accessibility statement to learn more about eBay's commitment to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities.




 We use cookies to enhance your experience and may use AI tools for administrative tasks in the hiring process. To learn how we handle your personal data and use AI responsibly, please visit our Talent Privacy Notice, Privacy Center, and AI Hiring Guidelines.
